<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Hippocrates is an 89-year-old physician and teacher with bilateral knee osteoarthritis and low bone mass, who comes for his subsequent annual wellness visit, a year after his last one at his previous practice. He has finished twelve weeks of physical therapy and has started a tai chi class twice a week. He walks into town for his teaching again, stopping once on the hill instead of three times. He has had no falls. He uses diclofenac gel on his knees most mornings and acetaminophen a few times a week. He sleeps about six and a half hours without a sleep aid and naps after lunch. His cold in the spring cleared in ten days. He had the pneumococcal vaccine six weeks ago. He wants to put in writing what he would and would not want if he became seriously ill. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Subsequent annual wellness visit, age 89</td></tr><tr><td>Mobility</td><td>Physical therapy finished; tai chi twice a week; no falls</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Diclofenac gel, acetaminophen as needed, vitamin D3 daily; no over-the-counter sleep aids or cold remedies</td></tr><tr><td>Mentation</td><td>Mini-Cog 5; PHQ-2 0</td></tr><tr><td>What matters</td><td>Teaching, walking into town, and living in his own house</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on paper at home and reviewed with him by Dr. Vasquez-Okafor at the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good for his age</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives alone; a neighbor looks in daily; pupils and friends visit; teaches two mornings a week</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>One small cup of watered wine with dinner (AUDIT-C 1); no other drugs</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks into town most days; tai chi twice a week; home exercises</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals; cheese and yogurt daily; weight steady</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Six and a half hours and an afternoon rest; no sleep aid</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in shopping, cooking, medicines and money</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Second stair rail and night lights fitted after the home safety check; smoke alarm working; no rugs on the stairs</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>No falls this year; one near-fall before intake; less fear of falling</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Hears conversation well; reading glasses; eye examination eight months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Continence</td><td>Gets up once at night to pass urine; no leakage</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

