    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment, functional and cognitive review (Mini-Cog 5), depression screen (PHQ-2 0), hearing and vision, falls and home safety reviewed, and the personalized prevention plan updated for a man of 89 whose aim is to keep teaching and living in his own house. Screening for cancers, diabetes, lipids, hepatitis C and HIV is not indicated at his age. [S]<list><item>RSV vaccine and the first recombinant zoster vaccine dose today; second zoster dose in two to six months; high-dose influenza vaccine in the autumn.</item><item>Eye examination yearly with his ophthalmologist.</item><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Primary osteoarthritis of both knees (M17.0)</content>. Pain 2 of 10 on the hill; independent; no falls. [S]<list><item>Continue tai chi and the home program.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>134/72 seated, 130/72 standing; no orthostatic fall</td></tr><tr><td>Falls risk (STEADI)</td><td>Up to date</td><td>At risk at intake; strength and balance program completed; repeat measures at the four-month review</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5; MoCA 26 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Whispered voice heard in both ears</td></tr><tr><td>Vision and eye examination</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Eye examination eight months ago; reading glasses</td></tr><tr><td>Osteoporosis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>DXA six weeks ago: low bone mass, FRAX below treatment thresholds; repeat in two years</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended after 85</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended at 70 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoked; beyond the age ranges</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes and lipid screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Beyond the screening age ranges; fasting glucose 92 mg/dL at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C and HIV screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Beyond the screening age ranges and no risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 1</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 six weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Single dose today (age 75 or older)</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First dose today; second in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>High-dose vaccine in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>This season&apos;s dose in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap eight years ago</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: RSV vaccine (adjuvanted RSVpreF3), single dose for an adult aged 75 or older; Recombinant zoster vaccine, first of two doses [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Age-Friendly Health Systems: the 4Ms (What Matters, Medication, Mentation, Mobility) (2026); Updating STEADI for Primary Care: Recommendations From the American Geriatrics Society Workgroup (2025); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Osteoporosis to Prevent Fractures: Screening (2025); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Four-month review in three weeks with repeat gait, balance and strength measures and vitamin D. Next annual wellness visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-06-29: four-month review: knee function, repeat gait, balance and strength measures, vitamin D, falls and the home program. [S]</paragraph></text>

